# CommitTrail environment variables
#
# Phase 1A requires NO environment variables — the application builds, tests,
# and runs without any of the entries below. Never commit a real .env file.

# --- Phase 1A · Optional GitHub token (active, optional) ---------------------
# Server-only. When set, public snapshot requests to the GitHub REST API are
# authenticated, which raises the rate limit. When unset, CommitTrail uses
# GitHub's anonymous public-data access. The token is never sent to the
# browser, never logged, never stored, and never required. Use a fine-grained
# token with NO scopes (public read only). Do not put a value in this file.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# --- Phase 2+ · Database (reserved, inactive) --------------------------------
# DATABASE_URL=

# --- Phase 2+ · Authentication (reserved, inactive) --------------------------
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=
# BETTER_AUTH_URL=

# --- Phase 2+ · GitHub App, read-only (reserved, inactive) -------------------
# GITHUB_APP_ID=
# GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY=
# GITHUB_APP_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_ID=
# GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Phase 4+ · Grounded drafting provider (reserved, inactive) --------------
# AI_PROVIDER_API_KEY=
